Karl Garrison <kdgarris@gmail.com> wrote:
> The discussion about vampires as a playable race in UnNetHack got me
> thinking about Slash`EM, and although I don't play Slash`EM much, one
> feature that I do like was the #technique command to access race and
> role-specific special abilities.  I think that this is a fun feature,
> and does much to differentiate the races and roles.
>
> So, I'm curious how people feel about Slash`EM techniques.  Does
> anyone have an interest in seeing a "port" of them to NetHack?  If so,
> would you change any of the specifics, or carry them over as-is?

I also think that just carry them over as-is would in would create an
overpowering problem for roles, races and combinations of roles and
races.

But also technically it would probably not be easy to just port the
whole technique code. You'd probably end up porting over half of
Slash'Em's inner framework.

It might be beneficial for role differentiation if some of the
techniques are ported over. I'm thinking about something like one
technique per role and none because of race.

For example "Blessing" for priests, "Research" for archaeologists, "Healing hands"
for knights would be really nice without being de-balancing. 
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Blessing
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Healing_hands
